Text: antacids that contain aluminum or magnesium - Gaviscon, Maalox, Milk of Magnesia, Mintox, Mylanta, Pepcid Complete, and others.
Tell your doctor about all your other medicines, especially:
orlistat;
phenobarbital, rifampin;
ketamine, steroid medicines such as dexamethasone;
antidepressants such as amitriptyline, maprotiline, or sertraline;
heart or blood pressure medication, including amiodarone, digoxin, propranolol, and other beta blockers;
furosemide given by injection;
seizure medicines such as carbamazepine or phenytoin;
high-dose aspirin, or anti-inflammatory painkillers;
estrogen, birth control pills, or tamoxifen;
testosterone or anabolic steroids;
diabetes medications, including insulin;
cancer medicine such as imatinib;
biotin or supplements that contain biotin; or
a blood thinner - warfarin, Coumadin, Jantoven.
If you have diabetes, levothyroxine can raise your blood sugar.
You may need more of your diabetes medicine or insulin.
Check your blood sugar more often when you start, change, or stop levothyroxine.
Tell your doctor about any changes.
Triplet: ["Levothyroxine", "has effect on", "blood sugar in diabetes"]

The relation 'has effect on' in the triplet is defined as 'The subject drug influences or alters the physiological parameter or condition specified by the object entity.' In this context, is there any relation appropriate to replace it? Choose a relation whose meaning and subject/object direction match the triplet even if the wording differs; choose 'None of the above' only if no candidate fits. Please answer by providing only the letter of your choice.

Choices:
A. 'improves': The subject drug enhances or positively affects the condition or parameter specified by the object entity.
B. 'acts in': The subject drug exerts its effects within the anatomical or physiological system specified by the object entity.
C. 'has effect': The subject drug produces the effect specified by the object entity.
D. 'interacts with': The subject drug has a drug interaction with the drug or substance specified by the object entity that may change effects or cause harm.
E. 'affects': The subject substance influences or alters the object entity, typically through biochemical or physiological mechanisms.
F. None of the above.

Answer:
